          ---
          THE CLAIM CHECKS OUT. The session note says Foot's geometric form is
          the square-root-mass vector at 45 degrees to (1,1,1). His abstract
          says only "this relation has a geometric interpretation", but the
          body is explicit: he defines theta as "the angle between this vector
          and the symmetric vector", notes that Koide's bound is
          cos theta > 1/sqrt(3), "which means that theta < 54.7 degrees", and
          concludes "theta = 45.000 +/- 0.001". So the 45 degrees, and the
          54.7 degree ceiling, are both his.}
